id: pm-web-4f52
title: "Deduplicate committed realtime facts across HTTP, watcher and peer delivery"
description: "PR #226 review corrections preserve exact committed identities across route, watcher and peer delivery. Current thread PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6uKnMQ is fixed by forwarding the invocation session through projectPm/runPm into the spawned CLI environment. Real-tracker tests verify durable episodes/provenance, distinct plan identities and manual SSE updates. After the required main dependency merge, targeted regressions pass 2/2 and runner/collaboration passes 18/18; function-only runner and route reversions produce the expected 2 and 1 assertion failures. Prior local npm timing failures and the full pre-merge Bun success remain in append-only comments and linked follow-up items. Exact pushed-head CI and fresh-clone health receipts are maintained in the PR #226 body. Leave in progress for orchestrator verification."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: capacity,realtime
created_at: "2026-10-19T17:45:22.211Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T03:52:47.529Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[30]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T18:20:50.917Z",codex-agent,"Investigating duplicate identities and delivery stages in an isolated package worktree based on the open capacity report. Plan: trace the 20-subscriber reproduction, add event-identity delivery receipts and only evidence-backed latency fixes, prove behavioral reverts, rerun the unchanged ladder and npm/Bun gates. No hosted access."
  "2026-10-19T18:20:51.102Z",codex-agent,"Tracing synthetic duplicate identities and latency stages in the package worktree; delivery receipts, behavioral revert proofs and unchanged capacity gates will be required. No hosted access."
  "2026-10-19T18:24:38.714Z",codex-agent,"20-subscriber trace reproduced 140 duplicates: HTTP write sequences 0,4,5,8,9,14,23 each had two socket writes per subscriber, first workspace-changed from mutation-events then item-updated from the route. This proves the watcher-before-route race in the one-shot item signal. NOTIFY self-echo, reconnect and harness double-counting are not the observed paths. Planned receipt identity is the committed item/version, shared across route, watcher and peer delivery."
  "2026-10-19T18:30:34.190Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof passed: keeping all other fixes and new tests, restoring only deliverProjectEvent from origin/main caused the 20-subscriber committed-version regression to fail (6 item frames instead of 2). Restoring the function passed. Covers watcher-first, route-first and peer-first deliveries, two distinct versions on the same item and real SDK history."
  "2026-10-19T18:36:06.938Z",codex-agent,Linked regression run passed 1/1 with real committed same-item versions and 20 subscribers in each delivery order. Peer identity validation plus trace tests passed 12/12. The fixed full ladder advanced beyond 100 subscribers; its final result is pending cleanup.
  "2026-10-19T18:54:52.768Z",codex-agent,"First full npm gate: 676/677 pass, one failure from adding version to the legacy HTTP SSE payload. Removing that unnecessary payload field preserves the existing contract; the receipt identity remains internal on SSEEvent and peer transport. Coverage floors were met (92.42 statements/lines, 81.57 branches, 96.17 functions). Focused compatibility and full gates will be rerun."
  "2026-10-19T18:58:33.627Z",codex-agent,Restored legacy HTTP payload plus receipt regression passed 9/9. Final untraced 100/1000 ladder again has zero duplicates and zero lost receipts (5000 and 50000 expected). The 1000 rung failed latency and stopped the ladder; dedup correctness is separate from capacity acceptance.
  "2026-10-19T19:51:48.885Z",codex-agent,"All source changes are verified by four complete CI gate runs at ad380c7, each 677/677 plus 2/2 capacity and 4/4 packed acceptance. SDK UX gap observed: PmClient.run mutation responses contain id/status/changed_field_count but no committed event identity, so safe route deduplication requires a follow-up committed-history read. No upstream issue filed."
  "2026-10-19T20:42:55.457Z",codex-agent,"PR #226 review round: verified all five unresolved threads against the current head; latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Plan: exact request-to-commit correlation, lifecycle delivery ordering, legacy one-shot compatibility, post-dedup trace accounting, and untraced reproduction command, each with regression and behavioural revert evidence. Node 22 CI failure is npm ECONNRESET during packed installation; revalidate without changing thresholds."
  "2026-10-19T20:45:19.028Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses the pinned SDK runWithAgentSessionContext to stamp a fresh request episode on committed history. Announcements match that exact episode before using an item/version receipt, preserving concurrent writers and authenticated display-name payloads. Watcher close/delete operations map to lifecycle event types; legacy callers retain one-shot fallback signals; tracing separates broadcast attempts from serialized emissions; the report now includes a fresh untraced ladder command. Regression validation and function-only revert runs are in progress."
  "2026-10-19T20:48:37.144Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proofs for PR #226: restore only traceDeliveries from the starting head -> emissions assertion fails (suppressed attempt counted as delivery); restore only consumeSignaledItemMutation -> legacy one-shot assertion fails; restore only createMutationEventReconciler -> watcher-first close lifecycle assertion fails; restore only emitItemEvent -> concurrency assertion fails with two item-closed announcements, including the independent writer version; restore only runMutation -> durable invocation assertion fails; restore only the report command block -> untraced ladder reproduction assertion fails. Each focused proof ran one test and produced one AssertionError failure, with no cancellation or skip. All files were restored. The fixed five new regressions passed 5/5 before the revert loop; rerunning the complete PM-linked suite now."
  "2026-10-19T20:51:58.509Z",codex-agent,"Restored PM-linked verification passed all 3 commands: realtime delivery 3/3, collaboration plus delivery 12/12, and collaboration/delivery/trace 18/18; zero failure, cancellation or skip. Typechecking, lint and zero-duplication checks pass. The unchanged full npm and Bun release gates now run sequentially with PM_FLEET_ROOT unset and isolated home/Git identity. Previous green CI counts in the description refer to the earlier accepted head, not this pending review correction."
  "2026-10-19T21:21:05.638Z",codex-agent,"Full isolated npm run release:check passed: 682/682 coverage tests, zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo, all 40 configured sources, statements/lines 92.42%, branches 81.72%, functions 96.19%, 2/2 capacity scenarios and 4/4 packed consumers, zero production vulnerabilities, and all static/changelog/date/publish-attestation checks. PM_FLEET_ROOT was unset, home and Git identity isolated, and no pins, thresholds, deadlines or assertions changed. The earlier CI ECONNRESET did not recur through the corresponding Bun-current packed installation. Full Bun gate is now running."
  "2026-10-19T21:49:53.171Z",codex-agent,"All five review fixes and six isolated revert proofs are complete. Full local npm gate is green (682/682, 2/2 capacity, 4/4 packed). Full local Bun coverage is green at 682/682 and unchanged floors, but its full gate failed the unchanged 2000 ms smoke SLO (1/2 capacity); its later stages were not reached. This failed receipt is preserved in the report and pm-web-h4vh. The unchanged focused workload subsequently passed at max/p99 490.9 ms with zero loss/duplicates; this does not establish the missed SLO root cause. Current-head CI must independently pass both full npm/Bun gates before completion."
  "2026-10-19T21:52:08.359Z",codex-agent,"Review implementation is complete: all five valid findings are fixed, six function/command reversions produce assertion failures, restored PM-linked suites pass 3/3, 12/12 and 18/18, and final trace/report checks pass 6/6. Full local npm passes all stages; full local Bun fails only the retained capacity SLO assertion after 682/682 coverage; unchanged isolated capacity retry passes 2/2. No thresholds or pins change. Releasing implementation claims while remote exact-head CI verification proceeds; the final remote gate receipts and pushed head are maintained at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/226. Items remain in progress for orchestrator verification. SDK UX gap: default mutation responses omit committed versions; immutable episode correlation supplies the safe join without a dependency change."
  "2026-10-19T22:52:17.910Z",codex-agent,"PR #226 review round: pulled the remote head 579a103 and confirmed origin/main is already an ancestor. Read all six review threads with every comment; only PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6uINkR remains unresolved. The latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Verified the watcher attaches only once, leaving later history-directory replacements unwatched. Plan: reattach from root directory notifications, preserve metadata polling, add real temporary-tracker regressions and function-only behavioural revert proof, then run unchanged npm and Bun release gates with isolated identity and PM_FLEET_ROOT unset. No hosted access."
  "2026-10-19T22:56:14.586Z",codex-agent,"Implemented root-triggered history watcher reattachment, closing the detached watcher before watching the current path. Metadata polling and its unchanged intervals remain the fallback. Two new real temporary-tracker regressions pass 2/2: history absent at attachment then created, and an existing history directory replaced while following. Both consume the directory notification before a separate pinned CLI process appends to an existing authoritative stream. Dependency install initially hit an inherited npm allow-scripts configuration refusal; retry with user npm config isolated passed without repository changes."
  "2026-10-19T22:56:34.063Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof for PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6uINkR: with both new regressions unchanged, restored only watchHistoryChanges from starting head 579a103. Exact command: env -u PM_FLEET_ROOT node --test --test-name-pattern=\"a later real append\" test/mutation-replay.test.ts. Both tests fail by AssertionError: undefined instead of reattach-one, because the later append does not wake the detached/missing watcher before the poll. Counts: 0/2 passed, 2 assertion failures, zero canceled/skipped/todo. The fixed function is restored; no SDK mock or generated-output change was needed because these tests import source. Initial fixed run passed 2/2. Strict tracker health now passes after the pinned install refreshed merge drivers; no pending merge receipts."
  "2026-10-19T23:01:40.920Z",codex-agent,"Final consolidated regression verification: pm test pm-web-4f52 --run --progress passed all four linked commands: delivery 3/3; collaboration plus delivery 12/12; collaboration, delivery and trace 18/18; history gate plus replay 10/10. Zero failures, canceled, skipped or todo tests. Tracker test-result tracking is disabled, so receipts are documented here without changing policy. Consolidated the pre-existing unchanged-directory wake test with created/replaced scenarios to retain the zero-duplication threshold. Final function-only revert proof repeats against this exact test: env -u PM_FLEET_ROOT node --test --test-name-pattern=\"a later real append.*(created|replaced)\" test/mutation-replay.test.ts -> 0/2 passed, two expected AssertionErrors, zero canceled/skipped/todo. Only watchHistoryChanges was restored from 579a103 and then restored to the fix. Existing timeouts, polling intervals, thresholds and pins remain unchanged. Lint, build and zero duplication pass."
  "2026-10-19T23:28:09.516Z",codex-agent,"Full isolated npm run release:check passes on the restored fix: 684/684 coverage tests, zero failed/canceled/skipped/todo, all 40 configured sources. Coverage is statements/lines 92.43%, branches 81.73%, functions 96.21%, above unchanged floors. Capacity passes 2/2, packed consumers pass 4/4 (npm/Bun current and minimum hosts), production audit has zero vulnerabilities, and all type/lint/duplication/docstring/changelog/date/publish-attestation checks pass. PM_FLEET_ROOT is unset and home plus Git identity are isolated. The complete Bun gate runs next without changing source, thresholds, pins or timeouts."
  "2026-10-19T23:47:57.130Z",codex-agent,"Full isolated bun run release:check also passes: 684/684 coverage tests, zero failed/canceled/skipped/todo, all 40 configured sources; statements/lines 92.45%, branches 81.73%, functions 96.21%. Capacity passes 2/2, packed consumers pass 4/4, production audit has zero vulnerabilities, and all type/lint/zero-duplication/docstring/changelog/date/publish-attestation checks pass. Both complete local gates now pass without source, dependency, threshold or timeout changes. Starting history remains an exact prefix; added tracked text passes local-path/network-address privacy checks. Only pm-web-4f52 is touched in this round. The original five resolved threads remain untouched; the one current unresolved finding is valid and fixed, with two regression assertions proven by function-only reversion. Exact-head CI and fresh-clone health verification follow before the final PR report; no thread replies or resolutions are authorized."
  "2026-10-20T00:45:23.163Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit Minor PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6uJ13N: removed the duplicated 'PR #226 review corrections' block (29 identical lines) from the PR #225 historical section of docs/capacity/2026-10-19-ladder.md; the current section at the top is unchanged."
  "2026-10-20T02:48:15.025Z",codex-agent,"PR #226 review round: fetched all threads and all unresolved comments; exactly one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6uKnMQ. Latest substantive CodeRabbit review 5579720351 has no Outside diff range findings. Remote branch is current and contains origin/main, so no merge or reconcile is needed. Verified that runMutation only propagates context in process and plan actions spawn without episode environment. Plan: pass the bounded agent session through projectPm/runPm to every fallback, cover real durable history and route plan updates with behavioural revert proofs, self-review the full PR diff, then run unchanged npm and Bun release gates with isolated git identity and disposable native PostgreSQL. Dependency installation needed user npm configuration disabled because allow-scripts breaks git dependency preparation; pins remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-20T02:50:56.507Z",codex-agent,"Verified PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6uKnMQ and fixed session transport through runMutation -> projectPm -> runPm -> runProcess environment using the pinned SDK agentSessionEnvironment helper. Both in-process dispatch and manual plan SSE broadcasts remain intact. Whole-PR self-review checked invocation identity, peer receipts, replay, watcher attachment and trace accounting; no additional instance needs a separate fix. Shared fallback transport also covers input/timeout/unsupported-dispatch fallbacks. Behavioural revert proofs: with both tests unchanged, reverting only runPm environment construction to starting head 06f37fe makes both regressions fail (0/2 pass, 2 AssertionErrors: missing durable episodes). Reverting only runMutation session forwarding makes the plan HTTP regression fail (0/1 pass, missing episode). Exact command for runner proof: env -u PM_FLEET_ROOT node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern=\"CLI fallbacks persist|plan fallback mutations\" test/pm-runner.test.ts test/pm-collaboration.test.ts. Route proof uses --test-name-pattern=\"plan fallback mutations\" test/pm-collaboration.test.ts. Tests import source, so no rebuild is required for these proofs. Fixed functions restored. Initial fixed targeted run passes 2/2 with zero skipped/canceled/todo."
  "2026-10-20T02:59:06.227Z",codex-agent,"Initial full linked-test run completed three commands successfully (delivery 3/3, collaboration plus delivery 13/13, history plus replay 10/10). Two commands hit the unchanged PM runner outer 120000 ms default while their child tests were still running; no assertion failures were reported. Tracker test-result tracking remains disabled, so these receipts are documented here without changing policy. Retry the timed-out commands separately after release-gate contention subsides; code, test deadlines, SLO and coverage floors remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-20T03:16:15.463Z",codex-agent,"Consolidated PM-linked verification is now green: delivery 3/3; collaboration plus delivery 13/13; collaboration, delivery and trace 19/19; history plus replay 10/10; runner plus collaboration 18/18. The two initially timed-out commands pass when rerun separately with pm test --only-index 3 --timeout 600 and pm test --only-index 5 --timeout 600. Only the PM outer command budget changes for these retries; every child test deadline and assertion is unchanged. No assertion failures, skips, canceled or todo tests remain in the accepted linked runs. The initial 120-second wrapper timeouts remain in prior comments. The isolated npm release gate is still running; it has reproduced existing catalog deadline and graph latency findings recorded on pm-web-qdhx and pm-web-hqqp."
  "2026-10-20T03:26:33.143Z",codex-agent,"Initial isolated npm run release:check exits nonzero during coverage: 686 tests, 683 passed, 2 failed, 1 canceled, zero skipped/todo. New route and runner regressions pass. Failures are the pre-existing built catalog 300000 ms timeout, follow-on source catalog startup failure, and the unchanged graph 10515 ms wall-time limit. Later release stages are not reached. Failed coverage reports are not accepted evidence; thresholds remain unchanged. Catalog/process details are tracked by pm-web-qdhx and graph by pm-web-hqqp. Running the complete isolated Bun gate next; no code change or deadline workaround is introduced."
  "2026-10-20T03:49:57.320Z",codex-agent,"Remote main advanced during long validation: required refresh now includes Dependabot PRs #227/#228 only (pm-graph 2026.10.16, pm-ops 2026.10.16, ESLint 10.13.0). The pinned PM CLI remains 2026.10.19 and release thresholds are unchanged. Finish the in-flight pre-merge Bun gate, commit the reviewed fix plus its tracker evidence, merge origin/main in the normal environment, reinstall the resulting pins, reconcile only if strict health reports pending receipts, then verify the merged implementation and exact pushed-head CI. Pre-merge local receipts are historical evidence and will not be presented as final-head dependency certification."
  "2026-10-20T03:50:40.958Z",codex-agent,"Complete pre-merge isolated bun run release:check exits 0: 686/686 coverage tests; zero failed/canceled/skipped/todo; all 40 configured sources; statements/lines 92.44%, branches 81.70%, functions 96.21%; 2/2 capacity scenarios; 4/4 packed npm/Bun current/minimum consumers; zero production vulnerabilities; all type, lint, zero-duplication, docstring, changelog, date and publish-attestation gates pass. Catalog built/source scenarios pass at 276872/251200 ms versus unchanged 300000 ms deadlines. The unchanged 2000-item graph read passes at 4272 ms wall, 2870 ms CPU. The earlier failed npm receipt remains preserved. These local gates precede the newly required main dependency merge; final exact-head release certification will come from both CI runtime jobs after the merge. No review-authored dependency or threshold change is introduced."
  "2026-10-20T03:52:46.835Z",codex-agent,"Merged origin/main at 900dc8a using normal repository merge drivers; merge commit 16ff41b changes only inherited dependency pins. Fresh npm ci installs the resulting pins, and strict health with required merge drivers passes with no pending receipts, so reconcile is not needed. Merged-code type checking, lint, zero duplication, docstrings and full build pass. Targeted regressions pass 2/2. Repeating the same function-only proofs with the merged dependencies gives runner 0/2 pass, 2 AssertionErrors for missing durable episodes, and route 0/1 pass, 1 AssertionError for missing plan episode. Fixed functions are restored; source imports need no rebuild for these reversions. Final pm test --only-index 5 --timeout 600 passes 18/18, zero failure/cancel/skip/todo. All five linked suites have passing receipts; earlier outer-wrapper timeouts remain recorded. Implementation is complete and the claim is released while exact pushed-head CI and fresh git clone --no-local health verification proceed. Their receipts will be maintained at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/226. No thread reply or resolution is authorized; item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
